;; it-fault-alias.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `it-fault-alias.s` (P2-SCALAR.4).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py it-fault-alias.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "it-fault-alias.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `it-fault-alias.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05), against the reference behaviors MEASURED by probe `alias-fault` (sail-riscv 0.14 AND" "spike 1.1.1-dev) before this guest existed. Fault × alias: the load's destination IS its base" "register. The trap step's EMPTY writes table is the observation that the base is preserved —" "the address is sampled before any write commits, and a trapping instruction retires no write," "so x5 keeps the lui's value through the fault.")
(expectations (program "it-fault-alias.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 2) (step (n 0) (insn "lui x5, 0x80000") (writes (write (reg "x5") (value "0xFFFFFFFF80000000"))) (derivation "0x80000 << 12 = 0x80000000 with bit 31 SET, so the U-immediate sign-extends: x5 = 0xFFFFFFFF80000000. The value is deliberately not the region base as a positive number — the load below must compute from the sign-extended value.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4 (D-LUI-AUIPC: the U-immediate sign-extends to 64 bits)")) (step (n 1) (insn "lw x5, x5, 1") (writes) (derivation "rd == rs1: the effective address 0xFFFFFFFF80000000 + 1 = 0xFFFFFFFF80000001 (1 mod 4, misaligned) is sampled from the base BEFORE any write commits, the misaligned load raises cause 0x04 with tval = the address — measured identical on both references (probe alias-fault) — and the write to x5 is SUPPRESSED: the empty writes table on a pre-written base is the observation that the base survives its own faulting load.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.6 (the EEI defines whether misaligned accesses are handled invisibly) — decision D-MISALIGN-DATA; RVI-RV64I §3.1.3")))
